hadiths[153]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20644","Abu Sa'id the freedman of Banu Hashim narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, Bahr ibn Marrar narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, he said: Abu Bakrah narrated to us, he said: While I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he holding my hand, with a man to his left, there we were before two graves ahead of us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are being punished, and they are not punished for a major matter, yet indeed. Which of you will bring me a palm stalk? We raced and I outran him and brought him a palm stalk. He broke it in halves, cast upon this grave a piece and upon this grave a piece, and said: It will be lightened for them as long as they remain moist. They are punished only for urine and backbiting."
"20645","Yahya narrated to us, from Uyaynah, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abu Bakrah, and Waki', he said: Uyaynah narrated to us, and Yazid, Uyaynah informed us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no sin more deserving that its punishment be hastened for its doer along with what is deferred for him in the Hereafter than oppression or severing kinship. Waki' said: that Allah hasten, and Yazid said: Allah hastens, and he said: along with what is stored for him."
"20646","Yahya narrated to us, from Uyaynah, and Waki', Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah, he said: We saw ourselves with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we were almost trotting with it. Waki' said: trotting with the funeral, trotting."
"20647","Waki' narrated to us, Uyaynah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Seek it in the last ten, with nine remaining, or seven remaining, or five, or three, or the last night."
"20648","Waki' and Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, they said: Uyaynah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a mu'ahid without its due course, Allah has forbidden him Paradise. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Its due course is right."
"20649","Waki' narrated to us, Zakariya Abu Imran, a Basran shaykh, narrated to us, he said: I heard a shaykh narrate from Ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a woman and dug for her to the than dwah, the upper chest."
"20650","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, that he wrote that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The judge shall not judge between two while he is angry."
"20651","Waki' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Rasibi narrated to us, from a freedman of Abu Bakrah, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two sins hastened, not deferred: oppression and severing kinship."
"20652","Waki' narrated to us, Uthman al-Shahham narrated to me, from Muslim ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from disbelief and poverty and the punishment of the grave."
"20653","Waki' narrated to us, Uthman Abu Salamah al-Shahham narrated to us, Muslim ibn Abi Bakrah narrated to me, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will emerge young, sharp, severe people with fluent tongues in the Qur'an. They will recite it not passing their collarbones. When you meet them then put them to rest, then when you meet them then kill them, for their killer will be rewarded."
"20654","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hakam ibn al-A'raj, from al-Ash'ath ibn Thurmallah, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a covenanted soul without its lawful right, Allah has forbidden him Paradise, to even find its scent."
"20655","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you think if Juhaynah and Aslam and Ghifar and Muzaynah are better with Allah than Banu Asad and Banu Tamim and Banu Abd Allah ibn Ghatafan and Banu Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah? A man said: They have failed and lost. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are better than Banu Tamim and Banu Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah and Banu Asad and Banu Abd Allah ibn Ghatafan."
"20656","Isma'il narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah narrated to us, from his father, he said: And Isma'il said once: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Shall I not inform you of the greatest of major sins, three times: associating with Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: And major sins were mentioned with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Associating with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and disobedience to parents, and he was reclining then sat up and said: And false testimony and false testimony and false testimony, or false speech and false testimony. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept repeating it until we said: Would that he fell silent."
"20657","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Bakrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed in his pilgrimage and said: Verily time has turned as its state on the day Allah created the heavens and the earth. The year is twelve months, of them four sacred: three consecutive, Dhu al-Qa'dah and Dhu al-Hijjah and al-Muharram, and Rajab of Mudar which is between Jumada and Sha'ban. Then he said: What day is this? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He fell silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. He said: Is it not the Day of Sacrifice? We said: Yes. Then he said: What month is this? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He fell silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. He said: Is it not Dhu al-Hijjah? We said: Yes. Then he said: What land is this? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He fell silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. He said: Is it not the Town? We said: Yes. He said: Your blood and your wealth, and I think he said: and your honors, are sacred to you as the sanctity of this day of yours in this month of yours in this land of yours. You will meet your Lord and He will ask you about your deeds. Verily do not return after me astray, striking the necks of one another. Have I conveyed? Let the witness among you convey to the absent, for perhaps one to whom it is conveyed will be more retentive of it than some who hear it. Muhammad said: And that was so; some to whom it was conveyed were more retentive of it than some who heard it."
"20658","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad meaning Ibn Sirin, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from Abu Bakrah, he said: When that day came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat upon a camel while a man held its rein or its halter. He said: What day is this day of yours? He said: So we fell silent until we thought he would name it other than its name. He said: Is it not the Sacrifice? He said: We said: Yes. He said: What month is this month of yours? He said: So we fell silent until we thought he would name it other than its name. He said: Is it not Dhu al-Hijjah? He said: We said: Yes. He said: What land is this land of yours? He said: So we fell silent until we thought he would name it other than its name. He said: Is it not the Town? He said: We said: Yes. He said: Your blood and your wealth and your honors among you are sacred as the sanctity of this day of yours in this month of yours in this land of yours. Let the witness convey to the absent, for the witness may convey it to one more retentive of it than him. Muhammad said: A man said: And that was so."
"20659","Hushaym narrated to us, from Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Bakrah, he said: We saw ourselves with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we would trot with the funeral, trotting."
"20660","Hushaym narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The judge shall not judge between two while he is angry."
"20661","Abd al-A'la and Rib'i ibn Ibrahim al-Ma'na narrated to us, they said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He stood dragging his garment hastily until he came to the mosque, and the people gathered. He prayed two rak'ahs and it cleared from it. Then he turned to us and said: The sun and the moon are two signs of the signs of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, by which He frightens His servants. They do not eclipse for the death of anyone. He said: And his son Ibrahim, peace be upon him, had died. When you see anything of them, pray and supplicate until what is with you of them is uncovered."
"20662","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that he narrated to him, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were with him. He leapt up alarmed dragging his garment, and he mentioned its meaning."
"20663","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Musa, also called Isra'il, he said: I heard al-Hasan say: I heard Abu Bakrah, and Sufyan said once: from Abu Bakrah: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the minbar with Hasan, peace be upon him, with him. He would turn to the people once and to him once, and say: This son of mine is a master, and perhaps Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will reconcile through him between two parties of the Muslims."
"20664","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is not proper for the judge, and Sufyan said once: for the ruler, to judge between two while he is angry."
"20665","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah narrated to us, from his father, he said: Major sins were mentioned with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Associating with Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and disobedience to parents, and he was reclining then sat up and said: And false testimony and false testimony, or false speech. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept repeating it until we said: Would that he fell silent. And he said once: al-Jurayri informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah narrated to us, from his father, he said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Shall I not inform you of the greatest of major sins: associating with Allah, Exalted, and he mentioned it."
"20666","Isma'il narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to buy silver for silver and gold for gold except like for like, and commanded us to buy silver for gold and gold for silver as we wish. Thabit ibn Ubayd said to him: Hand to hand? He said: Thus I heard."
"20667","Isma'il narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, he said: I heard Sa'd say: My ears heard and my heart retained that whoever claims to other than his father while knowing he is other than his father, Paradise is forbidden to him. He said: So I met Abu Bakrah and told him. He said: And my ears heard and my heart retained from Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"20668","Isma'il narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn al-A'raj, from al-Ash'ath ibn Thurmallah, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a covenanted soul without its lawful right, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has forbidden him Paradise; he will not smell its scent."
"20669","Isma'il narrated to us, Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no sin more deserving that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, hasten the punishment for its doer in this world along with what He stores for him in the Hereafter than oppression and severing kinship."
"20670","Isma'il narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, he said: I think it is from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Two months do not decrease: the two months of festival, Ramadan and Dhu al-Hijjah."
"20671","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Uyaynah, my father narrated to us, he said: I went out in the funeral of Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah. He said: Men of his family began to face the funeral walking backwards on their heels and saying: Gently, may Allah bless you. He said: Abu Bakrah caught up with us from the road of al-Mirbad. When he saw them and what they were doing, he charged at them on his mule and raised the whip at them and said: Make way, for by the One Who honored the face of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we saw ourselves with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we would almost trot with it. And Yahya said once: We saw ourselves with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"20672","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Uyaynah, my father narrated to me, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal is blind in the left eye; between his eyes is written Kafir, which the illiterate and the literate will read."
"20673","Yahya narrated to us, from Uyaynah, my father narrated to me, from Abu Bakrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A people who entrust their affair to a woman will never prosper."
"20674","Yahya narrated to us, from Uyaynah, my father narrated to me, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a mu'ahid without its due course, Allah has forbidden him Paradise, to even find its scent."
"20675","Yahya narrated to us, from Uyaynah, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I mentioned Laylat al-Qadr with Abu Bakrah. He said: I do not seek it except in the last ten, after something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I heard him say: Seek it in the last ten, with nine remaining, or seven remaining, or five remaining, or three remaining, or the last night."
"20676","Yahya narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, from Ziyad al-A'lam, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that he bowed before the row. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: May Allah increase you in eagerness, but do not repeat."
"20677","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Muhallab ibn Abi Habibah, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abu Bakrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let none of you say: I stood all of Ramadan and fasted it. He said: I do not know whether he disliked self-praise, or: there must be heedlessness or sleep."
"20678","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Qurrah narrated to us, Muhammad meaning Ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, and from another man, and he is in my view better than Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from Abu Bakrah, Abd Allah said: other than my father said: from Yahya in this hadith, I prefer in my view Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the people at Mina and said: Do you not know what day this is? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: So he fell silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. He said: Is it not the Day of Sacrifice? We said: Yes. He said: What land is this? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Is it not the Town? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Your blood and your wealth and your honors and your skins are sacred as the sanctity of this day of yours in this month of yours in this land of yours. Have I conveyed? We said: Yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness. Let the witness convey to the absent, for many a conveyed one conveys it to one more retentive of it than him. So it was so. And he said: Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another. When the day of the burning of Ibn al-Hadrami came, Jariyah ibn Qudamah burned him, he said: They looked down upon Abu Bakrah and said: This is Abu Bakrah. Abd al-Rahman said: My mother narrated to me that Abu Bakrah said: Had they entered upon me I would not have brandished a reed at them."
"20679","Yahya narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with these two rak'ahs and these two rak'ahs, so it was for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) four, and for them two rak'ahs each."
"20680","Waki' narrated to us, Uthman al-Shahham narrated to us, Muslim ibn Abi Bakrah narrated to us, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say after every prayer: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from disbelief and poverty and the punishment of the grave."
"20681","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you think if Juhaynah and Aslam and Ghifar are better than Banu Tamim and Banu Abd Allah ibn Ghatafan and Banu Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah, and he raised his voice with it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, they have failed and lost. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, they are better."
"20682","Waki' narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, from Bahr ibn Marrar, from Abu Bakrah, he said: I was walking with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he passed by two graves. He said: Who will bring me a palm stalk? He said: I raced, I and another man, and we brought an un stripped branch. He split it in two, placed upon this one one and upon this one one, then said: It will be lightened for them as long as there is anything of their moisture in them. Then he said: They are being punished for backbiting and urine."
"20683","Waki' narrated to us, Uthman al-Shahham narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Abi Bakrah narrated to me, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be a fitnah; the one lying down in it is better than the sitting, the sitting better than the standing, the standing in it better than the walking, and the walking better than the hastening. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command me? He said: Whoever has camels, let him join his camels; whoever has sheep, let him join his sheep; whoever has land, let him join his land; and whoever has nothing, let him go to his sword and strike its edge upon a rock, then let him escape if he can escape, then let him escape if he can escape."
"20684","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Awwam informed us, Sa'id ibn Jumhan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a land called al-Basrah, beside it a river called Dijlah with many palms, and the sons of Qantura' will descend upon it. The people will split into three groups: a group joining its origin and they perish, a group taking upon themselves and they disbelieve, and a group placing their offspring behind their backs and fighting; their slain are martyrs; Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will grant victory to their remainder. And Yazid doubted in it once and said: al-Busayrah or al-Basrah."
"20685","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jumhan, from Ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will indeed descend upon a land called al-Basrah or al-Busayrah, upon Dijlah a river, and he mentioned its meaning. Al-Awwam said: The sons of Qantura' are the Turks."
"20686","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are best? He said: One whose life is long and whose deed is good. He said: Which people are worst? He said: One whose life is long and whose deed is evil."
"20687","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: I fasted all of Ramadan and stood it all. Al-Hasan said: My father said, and Yazid said once: Qatadah said: Allah knows best, he feared self-praise for his ummah, or: there must be a sleeper or a heedless one."
"20688","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, from his father, he said: I mentioned Laylat al-Qadr with Abu Bakrah. He said: I do not seek it after what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say except in the last ten. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Seek it in the last ten, in its odd nights. He said: Abu Bakrah used to pray in the twenty of Ramadan as he prayed in the rest of the year, then when the ten entered he strove hard."
"20689","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two parents of the Dajjal will remain thirty years with no child born to them, then a one-eyed boy will be born to them, the most harmful thing and the least beneficial. His eyes sleep but his heart does not sleep. Then he described his parents and said: His father is a tall man with disproportioned flesh, long of nose as if his nose were a beak, and his mother a huge fleshy woman with great breasts. He said: We were told that a child of the Jews was born in Madinah. He said: I and al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam went until we entered upon his parents and saw in them the description of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And there he was wrapped in the sun in a velvet cloth of his, murmuring. We asked his parents and they said: We remained thirty years with no child born to us, then a one-eyed boy was born to us, the most harmful thing and the least beneficial. When we went out we passed by him and he said: What were you engaged in? We said: And you heard? He said: Yes, my eyes sleep but my heart does not sleep. And there he was Ibn Sayyad."
"20690","Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed on the Day of Sacrifice upon a she-camel of his. He said: He would speak here once and here once, with each people. Then he said: What day is this? He said: So we fell silent until we thought he would name it other than its name. He said: Is it not the Day of Sacrifice? He said: We said: Yes. Then he said: What month is this? He said: So we fell silent until we thought he would name it other than its name. He said: Then he said: Is it not Dhu al-Hijjah? He said: We said: Yes. Then he said: What land is this? He said: So we fell silent until we thought he would name it other than its name. He said: Then he said: Is it not the sacred Town? He said: We said: Yes. He said: Your blood and your wealth and your honors are sacred to you until you meet your Lord, Exalted, as the sanctity of this day of yours in this month of yours in this land of yours. Then he said: Let the witness among you convey to the absent, for perhaps the absent will be more retentive of it than the witness."
"20691","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ziyad al-A'lam, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began the prayer and said takbir, then gestured to them: Stay in place. Then he entered and came out with his head dripping, and prayed with them. When he completed the prayer he said: I am only a human, and I was junub."
"20692","Mu'ammal narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your forerunner at the Hawd."
"20693","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that they mentioned a man with him. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, there is no man after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) better than him in such-and-such. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to you, you have cut the neck of your companion, repeatedly saying that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you must praise his brother, let him say: I deem so-and-so, if he sees that he is so, and I do not declare anyone pure before Allah, Blessed and Exalted; Allah is his reckoner, I deem him such-and-such."
"20694","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ya'qub al-Dabbi, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah narrate from his father that al-Aqra' ibn Habis came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Only the thieves of pilgrims pledged allegiance to you, of Aslam and Ghifar and Muzaynah, and I think Juhaynah, Muhammad is the one who doubts. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you think if Aslam and Ghifar and Muzaynah, and I think Juhaynah, are better than Banu Tamim and Banu Amir and Asad and Ghatafan, have they failed and lost? He said: Yes. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, they are indeed better than them, they are indeed better than them."
"20695","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Abu Bakrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When two Muslims, one of them raises arms against his companion, they are upon the edge of Hell. When one of them kills his companion, they enter it together."
"20696","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Jibril and Mika'il, peace be upon them, came to me. Jibril, peace be upon him, said: Recite the Qur'an upon one harf. Mika'il said: Ask for more. He said: Recite it upon seven ahruf, all healing sufficient, so long as a verse of mercy is not sealed with punishment or a verse of punishment with mercy."
"20697","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ziyad al-A'lam, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Fajr prayer and gestured to them: Stay in place. He went then came with his head dripping, and prayed with them."
"20698","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: I stood all of Ramadan."
"20699","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Talhah ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The people spoke much about Musaylimah before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said anything about him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood as a preacher and said: To proceed, concerning this man about whom you have spoken much, he is a liar among thirty liars who will emerge before the Hour. There is no town but the terror of the Masih will reach it except Madinah; upon every pass of its passes are two angels repelling from it the terror of the Masih."
"20700","Abu al-Nadr and Affan narrated to us, they said: al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, he said: Affan said in his hadith: al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan say: Abu Bakrah informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon people passing an unsheathed sword among themselves. He said: May Allah curse whoever did this. Have I not forbidden this? Then he said: When one of you draws his sword and looks at it, and wants to hand it to his brother, let him sheathe it, then hand it to him."
"20701","Abu Amir told us, Abd al-Jalil told us, Jafar ibn Maymun told me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah told me that he said to his father: O my father, I hear you supplicate every morning: O Allah, grant me health in my body, O Allah, grant me health in my hearing, O Allah, grant me health in my sight, there is no god but You, you repeat it three times when you enter the morning and three times when you enter the evening, and you say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from disbelief and poverty, O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, there is no god but You, you repeat it when you enter the morning three times and three times when you enter the evening. He said: Yes, my son, I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicating with them, so I love to follow his Sunnah."
"20702","He said, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The supplications of the distressed: O Allah, Your mercy I hope for, so do not entrust me to myself for the blink of an eye, set right for me all my affair, there is no god but You."
"20703","Rawh told us, Uthman al-Shahham told us, Muslim ibn Abi Bakrah told us, from his father, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man prostrating while he was going to the prayer, then he finished the prayer and returned to him while he was prostrating. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said: Who will kill this one? So a man stood and bared his hands and drew his sword and shook it, then said: O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, how can I kill a man prostrating who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger? Then he said: Who will kill this one? So a man stood and said: I will, and he bared his forearms and drew his sword and shook it until his hand trembled, then said: O Prophet of Allah, how can I kill a man prostrating who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if you had killed him, it would have been the first fitnah and the last of it."
"20704","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Tayalisi Abu Dawud told us, Imran informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, meaning: Fast at sighting the crescent and break fast at sighting it, and if it is obscured from you, then complete the count as thirty, and the month is like this and like this and like this, and he folded (his fingers)."
"20705","Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, Humayd ibn Mihran told us, Sad ibn Aws told us, from Ziyad ibn Kusayb al-Adawi, from Abu Bakrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever honors the authority of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, in this world, Allah will honor him on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever degrades the authority of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, in this world, Allah will degrade him on the Day of Resurrection."
"20706","Abd al-Samad and Affan said, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, Affan said, Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from Bilal ibn Yaqtar, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought dinars, and he began taking handful after handful, then looking to his right as if consulting someone, then giving, while a black man with a shaved head, wearing two white garments, with a mark of prostration between his eyes, said: You have not been just in the division. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and said: Who will be just over you after me? They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not kill him? He said: No. Then he said to his companions: This one and his companions pass through the religion as the arrow passes through the target, they do not attach to Islam in anything."
"20707","Abd al-Samad told us, Bashshar al-Khayyat told us, he said: I heard Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Bakrah narrating that Abu Bakrah came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was bowing, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the sound of Abu Bakrah's shoes as he was hurrying, wanting to catch the rakah. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: Who was the one hurrying? Abu Bakrah said: I was. He said: May Allah increase you in eagerness, and do not repeat."
"20708","Abd al-Samad told us, Zakariyya ibn Sulaym al-Muqri told us, he said: I heard a man narrating to Amr ibn Uthman, while I was present, that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah narrating that Abu Bakrah narrated to them that he witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing upon his mule when they brought a pregnant woman, and she said that she had committed adultery, so stone her. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Cover yourself with the cover of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. So she went back, then she came a second time while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon his mule, and said: Stone her, O Prophet of Allah. So he said: Cover yourself with the cover of Allah, Blessed and Exalted. So she went back, then she came a third time while he was standing, until she took hold of the bridle of his mule and said: I adjure you by Allah that you stone her. So he said: Go until you give birth. So she left and gave birth to a boy, then she came and spoke to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he said to her: Go and purify yourself from the blood. So she left, then she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said that she had become purified. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent women and commanded them to examine the woman, and they came and testified before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to her purity. So he ordered a pit for her up to her chest, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with the Muslims, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a pebble like a chickpea and threw it, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned aside and said to the Muslims: Stone her, but beware of her face. When she died, he ordered her to be taken out, and he prayed over her, then said: If her reward were divided among the people of the Hijaz, it would encompass them."
"20709","Attab ibn Ziyad told us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, Zakariyya Abu Imran al-Basri informed us, he said: I heard a shaykh narrating to Amr ibn Uthman al-Qurashi, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah told us, then he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took responsibility for him (the child), and said: If her reward were divided among the people of the Hijaz, it would encompass them."
"20710","Aswad ibn Amir told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that a man from the people of Persia came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My lord, Blessed and Exalted, has killed your lord, meaning Kisra. He said: And it was said to him, meaning to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he had appointed his daughter as successor. So he said: A people will not prosper whom a woman rules."
"20711","Muammal ibn Ismail told us, Hammad ibn Zayd told us, al-Mualla ibn Ziyad and Yunus and Ayyub and Hisham told us, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two Muslims confront one another with their swords, and one of them kills his companion, then the killer and the killed are in the Fire. It was said: This is the killer, so what about the killed? He said: He had intended to kill his companion."
"20712","Affan told us, Said ibn Zayd told us, he said: I heard Abu Sulayman al-Asari, Uqbah ibn Suhban told me, he said: I heard Abu Bakrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The people will be carried over the Sirat on the Day of Resurrection, and the sides of the Sirat will shake them off as moths are shaken into the Fire. He said: Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will save by His mercy whom He wills. He said: Then permission will be given to the angels and the prophets and the martyrs to intercede, so they will intercede and bring out, and intercede and bring out, and intercede and bring out, and Affan once added, and he also said: And they will intercede and bring out whoever had in his heart the weight of a speck of faith."
"20713","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Muhammad ibn Aban told us, Said ibn Zayd told us the like of it."
"20714","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi told us, Ibrahim ibn Sad informed us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The terror of the Masih al-Dajjal will not enter Madinah; it will have on that day seven gates, upon each gate two angels."
"20715","Yaqub told us, my father told us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Bakrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned the like of it."
"20716","Yunus ibn Muhammad told us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, told us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is best? He said: Whose life is long and whose deed is good. He said: Then which of the people is worst? He said: Whose life is long and whose deed is evil."
"20717","Yunus, meaning Ibn Muhammad, told us, Hammad told us, from Yunus and Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"20718","Abd al-Samad told us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, told us, Ali ibn Zayd told us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, he said: I came as a delegate with my father to Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, and we were admitted to him, and he said: O Abu Bakrah, narrate to me something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like the righteous dream and ask about it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: Which of you has seen a dream? So a man said: I, O Messenger of Allah, saw as if a scale was let down from the sky, and you were weighed against Abu Bakr, and you outweighed Abu Bakr, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, then Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, was weighed against Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and Abu Bakr outweighed Umar, then Umar was weighed against Uthman, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, and Umar outweighed Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them, then the scale was lifted, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) showed displeasure at it. So he said: Caliphate of prophethood, then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will give kingship to whom He wills. My father said: Affan said in it: So he showed displeasure at it. He said: And Hammad said: So that grieved him."
"20719","Rawh told us, Uthman al-Shahham told us, Muslim ibn Abi Bakrah told us, and he asked him whether he had heard anything about the Khawarij, so he said: I heard my father Abu Bakrah saying, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Indeed, there will emerge from my Ummah peoples, severe, sharp, with tongues fluent in the Quran, it will not pass beyond their throats. Indeed, when you see them, kill them, then when you see them, kill them, for the one who kills them will be rewarded."
"20720","Rawh told us, Uthman al-Shahham told us, Muslim ibn Abi Bakrah told me that he passed by his father while he was supplicating and saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from disbelief and poverty and the punishment of the grave. He said: So I learned them from him, and I used to supplicate with them at the end of every prayer. He said: So he passed by me while I was supplicating with them, and said: O my son, from where did you learn these words? He said: O my father, I heard you supplicating with them at the end of every prayer, so I learned them from you. He said: Then keep to them, my son, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with them at the end of every prayer."
"20721","Hashim told us, al-Mubarak told us, al-Hasan told us, Abu Bakrah told us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray with the people, and al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to jump on his back when he prostrated, and he did that more than once. So they said to him: By Allah, you do with this one something we have not seen you do with anyone. Al-Mubarak said: Then he mentioned something, then said: This son of mine is a master, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will reconcile through him between two groups of the Muslims. Al-Hasan said: So by Allah, by Allah, after he assumed authority, there was not shed in his caliphate even a cupping-glassful of blood."
"20722","Aswad ibn Amir told us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, and from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Bakrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another. And Ibn Sirin said: Astray, striking the necks of one another."
"20723","Aswad ibn Amir told us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, and from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Bakrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another. And Ibn Sirin said: Astray, striking the necks of one another."
"20724","Hashim ibn al-Qasim told us, Shubah told us, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Said, he said: I heard a freedman of the family of Abu Musa al-Ashari, kunya Abu Abdullah, he said: I heard Said ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Basri narrating from Abu Bakrah that he was once called to testify, so he came to the house, and a man stood up for him from his seat, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us, when a man stands for a man from his seat, that he sit in it, and that a man wipe his hand with the garment of one he does not own."
"20725","Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim told us, al-Hashraj ibn Nubatah al-Qaysi al-Kufi told us, Said ibn Jumhan told me, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakrah told us, my father told me in this mosque, meaning the mosque of Basrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A group of my Ummah will certainly settle in a land called Basrah, their number will be many therein and their date-palms many therein, then the Banu Qantura will come, broad-faced, small-eyed, until they settle upon a bridge of theirs called Dijlah, and the Muslims will split into three groups: As for one group, they will take hold of the tails of camels and join the desert, and they will perish. And as for a group, they will take to themselves and disbelieve, so this one and that one are alike. And as for a group, they will place their families behind their backs and fight, so their slain are martyrs, and Allah will grant victory to the rest of them."
"20726","Surayj told us, Hashraj told us, from Said, from Abdullah or Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakrah, he said: My father told me in this mosque, meaning the mosque of Basrah, then he mentioned the like of it."
"20727","Hawdhah ibn Khalifah told us, Abdullah ibn Awn told us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from Abu Bakrah, he said: When that day came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted his she-camel, then stood and said: Do you know what day this is? Then he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Ibn Abi Adiyy, and he said in it: Let the witness convey to the absent, twice, for perhaps one conveyed to is more retentive than one who conveys the like of it. Then he leaned toward his she-camel to some small sheep and began dividing them between two men a sheep and three men a sheep."
"20728","Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad told us, he said: I heard Hammad ibn Salamah narrating from Ali ibn Zayd and Humayd, among others, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will support this religion with peoples who have no share in it."
"20729","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Harrani told us, Abu Bakrah Bakkar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Bakrah told us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Bakrah that he witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a bearer of glad tidings came to him bringing him glad tidings of the victory of an army of his over their enemy, while his head was in the lap of Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her. So he stood and fell prostrate, then he began questioning the bearer of glad tidings, and he informed him, among what he informed him, that a woman had assumed authority over them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Now men are ruined when women are obeyed, men are ruined when women are obeyed, three times."
"20730","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik told us, Bakkar told us, he said: My father told me, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shows off, Allah will expose him, and whoever seeks reputation, Allah will give him reputation."
"20731","Affan told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, Ziyad al-Alam informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that he came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was bowing, so he bowed before the row, then walked to the row. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is this who bowed then walked to the row? So Abu Bakrah said: I did. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah increase you in eagerness, and do not repeat."
"20732","Affan told us, Hammam told us, Ziyad al-Alam informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that he entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was bowing, so he bowed before reaching the row. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: May Allah increase you in eagerness, and do not repeat."
"20733","Affan told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, Ziyad al-Alam informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Fajr prayer and gestured to his companions, meaning stay in your place, then he went and came back with his head dripping, and prayed with the people."
"20734","Ali ibn Abdullah told us, Muadh ibn Muadh told us, Shubah told us, Fudayl ibn Fudalah told me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah told me, he said: Abu Bakrah saw people praying Duha, so he said: They are praying a prayer that neither the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nor most of his companions, may Allah be pleased with them, prayed."
"20735","Affan told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan and Muhammad, from Abu Bakrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."
"20736","Affan told us, Wuhayb and Yazid, meaning Ibn Zuray, said, Khalid al-Hadhdha told us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from Abu Bakrah, he said: A man praised a man before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to you, you have cut the neck of your companion, several times. When one of you must praise his companion, let him say: I think so-and-so, and Allah is his Reckoner, and I do not declare anyone pure before Allah, Blessed and Exalted, if he knows that of him, I think him such-and-such."
"20737","Affan told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, Thabit informed us, that Abu Bakrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade khadhf (flinging pebbles). Then a cousin of his took and said about this and flung pebbles. So he said: Do I see you, I inform you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade it, yet you fling pebbles? By Allah, I will not speak to you as a firm resolve as long as I live, or as long as I remain, or the like of this."
"20738","Hajjaj told us, Layth told us, Uqayl told me, from Ibn Shihab, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, that Iyad ibn Musafi informed him, from Abu Bakrah, brother of Ziyad through his mother, Abu Bakrah said: The people spoke much about Musaylimah the liar before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said anything about him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among the people and praised Allah, Blessed and Exalted, as He deserves, then said: As for what follows, indeed the affair of this man about whom you have spoken much, he is a liar among thirty liars who will emerge before the Dajjal, and there is no land but the terror of the Masih will enter it except Madinah; upon each mountain pass of its passes on that day will be two angels repelling from it the terror of the Masih."
"20739","Yaqub told us, Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab told us, from his uncle, Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf informed me, that Iyad ibn Musafi narrated to him, that Abu Bakrah, brother of Ziyad through his mother, said: Abu Bakrah said: The people spoke much about Musaylimah, then he mentioned the like of it."
"20740","Hushaym informed us, Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, from Abu Uthman, he said: When Ziyad claimed (a different father), I met Abu Bakrah and said: What is this that you have done? I heard Sad ibn Abi Waqqas saying: My ears heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he says: Whoever claims a father in Islam other than his father, Paradise is forbidden to him. So Abu Bakrah said: And I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"20741","Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi told us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr told us, Ibn Abi Bakrah told me, that his father ordered him to write to a son of his who was a judge in Sijistan: As for what follows, do not judge between two persons while you are angry, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No one should judge between two while he is angry."
"20742","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, Ibn Abi Bakrah told us, from Abu Bakrah, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man praised a man, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have cut his back. When one of you must praise his companion, let him say: I think him, and Allah is his Reckoner, and I do not excuse anyone before Allah, I think him such-and-such, if he knows that of him."
"20743","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah and more than one, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The scent of Paradise is found from a distance of a hundred years, and there is no servant who kills a covenanted soul but Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has forbidden him Paradise and its scent to find it. Abu Bakrah said: May Allah deafen my ear if I did not hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying it."
"20744","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, that Abu Bakrah entered the mosque while the Imam was bowing, so he bowed before reaching the row. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: May Allah increase you in eagerness, and do not repeat."
"20745","Abd al-Razzaq told us, Mamar told us, he said: I heard Hisham narrating from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, the like of it."
"20746","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two Muslims confront one another with their swords, and one of them kills his companion, then the killer and the killed are in the Fire. They said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the killer, so what about the killed? He said: He wanted to kill his companion."
"20747","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed me, from one who heard al-Hasan narrating from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to narrate to us one day while al-Hasan ibn Ali was in his lap, and he would turn to his companions and narrate to them, then turn to al-Hasan and kiss him, then said: This son of mine is indeed a master; if he lives, he will reconcile between two groups of the Muslims."
"20748","Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, Uyaynah told us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A people will never prosper who entrust their affair to a woman."
"20749","Muhammad ibn Bishr told us, Misar told us, Sad ibn Ibrahim told us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The terror of the Masih al-Dajjal will not enter Madinah; it will have on that day seven gates, for each gate two angels."
"20750","Abd al-Ala told us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The people spoke much about Musaylimah, then he mentioned similar to the hadith of Uqayl."
"20751","Yazid ibn Harun told us, Uyaynah informed us, from his father, from Abu Bakrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A people will not prosper who entrust their affair to a woman."
"20752","Yazid ibn Harun told us, Mubarak ibn Fudalah told us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A people will not prosper whom a woman rules."
"20753","Yazid ibn Harun told us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, and Rawh told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, from Salim Abu Hatim, and Rawh said, from Salim Abu Ubaydullah ibn Salim, my father said, and Affan told us in a hadith he mentioned, from Hammad, from Salim Abu Ubaydullah, and he is also kunya Abu Hatim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Two months of Eid do not decrease: Ramadan and Dhu al-Hijjah."
"20754","Yazid told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which of the people is most excellent, or he said best, Yazid doubted. He said: Whose life is long and whose deed is good. It was said: Then which of the people is worst? He said: Whose life is long and whose deed is evil."
"20755","Rawh told us, Hammad told us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is best? He said: Whose life is long and whose deed is good. It was said: Then which of the people is worst? He said: Whose life is long and whose deed is evil."
"20756","Rawh told us, Hammad told us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"20757","Rawh and Abu Dawud said, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, Abu Dawud said, Ali ibn Zayd told us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed Isha seven nights, Abu Dawud said, eight nights, until a third of the night. So Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, if you would hasten, it would be better for our standing in the night. He said: Then he hastened after that. My father said, and Abd al-Samad told us, and he said in his hadith: Seven nights, and Affan said: Nine nights."
"20758","Mahbub ibn al-Hasan told us, from Khalid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, that a man praised a companion of his before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Woe to you, you have cut his neck. If you must praise, say: I think him such-and-such, and Allah is his Reckoner, and I do not declare anyone pure before Allah the Exalted."
"20759","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us, Shubah told us, he said: I heard Khalid al-Hadhdha narrating from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Two months do not decrease, in each of them an Eid: Ramadan and Dhu al-Hijjah."
"20760","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us, Shubah told us, and Hajjaj said, I heard Shubah, he said: I heard Abd Rabbihi ibn Said, and Bahz said, Abd Rabbihi, narrating from Abu Abdullah, freedman of Abu Musa, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan, he said: Abu Bakrah came to us regarding a testimony, and a man stood up for him from his seat, so Abu Bakrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man should not make a man stand from his seat then sit in it, or he said: When a man makes a man stand from his seat, he should not sit in it, and a man should not wipe his hand with the garment of one he does not own."
"20761","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us, Shubah told us, from Abu Bishr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Aslam and Ghifar and Muzaynah and Juhaynah are better than Banu Tamim and Banu Amir."
"20762","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us, Said told us, and Abd al-Wahhab, from Said, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should say: I stood (in prayer) all of Ramadan. He said: So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, knows best, I fear he disliked self-praise for his Ummah. Abd al-Wahhab said: So Allah knows best, I fear praise for his Ummah, or he said: There must be sleep or heedlessness."
"20763","Yazid informed us, Hammam informed us, and Affan told us, Hammam told us, Qatadah informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should say: I stood all of Ramadan. Qatadah said: So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, knows best, I fear praise for his Ummah. Affan said: Or he said: There must be one sleeping or heedless."
"20764","Rawh told us, Uthman al-Shahham told us, Muslim ibn Abi Bakrah told us, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There will be tribulations, then there will be tribulations. Indeed, the one walking therein is better than the one hastening to them. Indeed, the one sitting therein is better than the one standing therein. Indeed, the one lying down therein is better than the one sitting. Indeed, when they descend, whoever has sheep, let him join his sheep. Indeed, whoever has land, let him join his land. Indeed, whoever has camels, let him join his camels. So a man from the people said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make me ransom for you, what about one who has no sheep nor land nor camels, what should he do? He said: Let him take his sword, then let him go to a rock, then let him strike its edge with a stone, then let him escape if he can escape. O Allah, have I conveyed, O Allah, have I conveyed. When a man said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make me ransom for you, what if I am taken by my hand, coerced, until I am brought to one of the two ranks or one of the two groups, Uthman doubted, and a man stabs me with his sword and kills me, what will be my case? He said: He will bear your sin and his sin, and will be among the companions of the Fire."
"20765","Sulayman ibn Dawud told us, Shubah told us, Ali ibn Zayd informed me, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah narrating from his father, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is best? He said: Whose life is long and whose deed is good. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is worst? He said: Whose life is long and whose deed is evil."
"20766","Abu Nuaym told us, Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah told us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which of the people is best? Then he mentioned the like of it."
"20767","Abd al-Samad told us, Said Abu Uthman al-Shahham told us, in Murabbah al-Ahnaf, Muslim ibn Abi Bakrah told us, from his father, he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When two Muslims fight one another, then the killer and the killed are in the Fire."
"20768","Affan told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Men among those who accompanied me and saw me will certainly come to my Hawd, until when they are raised to me and I see them, they will be snatched away from me. So I will surely say: My Lord, my companions, my companions. So it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"20769","Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, Humayd ibn Mihran al-Kindi told us, Sad ibn Aws told me, from Ziyad ibn Kusayb al-Adawi, from Abu Bakrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever honors the authority of Allah in this world, Allah will honor him on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever degrades the authority of Allah in this world, Allah will degrade him on the Day of Resurrection."
"20770","Ismail told us, Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq told me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah told us, he said: Abu Bakrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to buy silver for silver and gold for gold except equal for equal, and commanded us to buy silver for gold and gold for silver as we wish. So Thabit ibn Abdullah said to him: Hand to hand? So he said: Thus I heard."
"20771","Rawh told us, Ashath told us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the fear prayer, so he prayed with some of his companions two rakahs, then gave salam, and they moved back, and others came and stood in their place, and he prayed with them two rakahs, then gave salam. So for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) it was four rakahs, and for the people two rakahs each."
"20772","Abu Amir told us, Qurrah ibn Khalid told us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah told me, from his father, and a man in my mind better than Abd al-Rahman, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on the Day of Sacrifice and said: What day is this? Or he said: Do you know what day this is? He said: We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Then he fell silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. Then he said: Is it not the Day of Sacrifice? He said: We said: Yes. He said: Then what month is this? Or he said: Or do you know what month this is? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Then he fell silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. He said: Is it not Dhu al-Hijjah? We said: Yes. He said: What land is this? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Then he fell silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. He said: Is it not the Town? We said: Yes. He said: Then your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you as the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours, until the day you meet your Lord, Blessed and Exalted. Indeed, have I conveyed? They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness. Let the witness convey to the absent, for perhaps one conveyed to is more retentive than one who heard. Indeed, do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."
"20773","Muammal told us, Hammad ibn Zayd told us, Ali ibn Zayd told us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was one day preaching, al-Hasan ibn Ali came and climbed to him upon the minbar, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew him to himself and wiped over his head and said: This son of mine is a master, and perhaps Allah will reconcile through his hands between two great groups of the Muslims."
"20774","Affan told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from Abu Bakrah, and Humayd and Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is best? He said: Whose life is long and whose deed is good. He said: Then which of the people is worst? He said: Whose life is long and whose deed is evil."
"20775","Hasan told us, Hammad told us, from Thabit and Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, then he mentioned it. Affan told us, Hammad told us, from Thabit and Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, then he mentioned it."
"20776","Affan told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parents of the Dajjal will remain thirty years without a child being born to them, then a boy will be born to them, the most harmful thing and the least beneficial. His eyes sleep but his heart does not sleep. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described his father and said: His father is a tall man, lean of flesh, as if his nose is a beak, and his mother is a bulky woman, long-breasted. Abu Bakrah said: So we heard of a newborn born among the Jews in Madinah, so I went with al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam until we entered upon his parents, and there was the description of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in them. So we said: Do you have a child? So they said: We remained thirty years without a child being born to us, then a one-eyed boy was born to us, the most harmful thing and the least beneficial. His eyes sleep but his heart does not sleep. So we left them, and there was the boy lying wrapped in a velvet cloth in the sun, humming. He said: So I uncovered his head, and he said: What did you two say? We said: Did you hear? He said: Yes, my eyes sleep but my heart does not sleep. Hammad said: And he is Ibn Sayyad."
"20777","Affan told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, he said: We came as a delegation with Ziyad to Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, and among us was Abu Bakrah. When we came to him, he was not pleased with a delegation as he was pleased with us. So he said: O Abu Bakrah, narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like the good dream and ask about it. So he said one day: Which of you has seen a dream? So a man said: I saw as if a scale was let down from the sky, and you were weighed against Abu Bakr, and you outweighed Abu Bakr, then Abu Bakr was weighed against Umar, and Abu Bakr outweighed Umar, then Umar was weighed against Uthman, and Umar outweighed Uthman, then the scale was lifted, and he showed displeasure at it, and Hammad also said: So that grieved him. Then he said: Caliphate of prophethood, then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will give kingship to whom He wills. He said: So we were pushed from behind our necks and expelled. So Ziyad said: May you have no father, did you not find a hadith other than this? Narrate to him other than this. He said: No, by Allah, I will not narrate to him except this until I part from him. So he left us, then he called us and said: O Abu Bakrah, narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So he repeated it to him, and we were pushed from behind our necks and expelled. So Ziyad said: May you have no father, do you not find a hadith other than this? Narrate to him other than this. So he said: No, by Allah, I will not narrate to him except with it until I part from him. He said: Then he left us for days, then he called us and said: O Abu Bakrah, narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So he repeated it to him, so Muawiyah said: Do you say kingship? For we are content with kingship."
"20778","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I found these hadiths in my father's book in his handwriting: Hawdhah ibn Khalifah told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from Abu Bakrah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the best of the people? He said: Whose life is long and whose deed is good. He said: Then which of the people is worst? He said: Whose life is long and whose deed is evil."
"20779","And with its isnad, and Abd al-Rahman said: We came as a delegation to Muawiyah to offer condolences with Ziyad, and with us was Abu Bakrah. When we arrived, he was not pleased with a delegation as he was pleased with us. So he said: O Abu Bakrah, narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like the good dream and ask about it, and he said one day: Which of you has seen a dream? So a man from the people said: I saw a scale let down from the sky, and you were weighed in it against Abu Bakr, and you outweighed Abu Bakr, then Abu Bakr was weighed in it against Umar, and Abu Bakr outweighed Umar, then Umar was weighed in it against Uthman, and Umar outweighed Uthman, then the scale was lifted, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) showed displeasure at it, meaning he interpreted it. So he said: Caliphate of prophethood, then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will give kingship to whom He wills. He said: So we were pushed from behind our necks and expelled. When the next day came, we returned, so he said: O Abu Bakrah, narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So he repeated it to him, and we were pushed from behind our necks. When on the third day we returned, and he asked him also, he said: So he repeated it to him, so Muawiyah said: You say we are kings; we are content with kingship."
"20780","And Abu Bakrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a covenanted soul without its right will not find the scent of Paradise, and its scent is indeed found from a distance of five hundred years."
"20781","And Abu Bakrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Men among those who accompanied me and saw me will certainly come to the Hawd before me, and when they are raised to me and I see them, they will be snatched away from me. So I will surely say: My little companions, my little companions. So it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"20782","And Abu Bakrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who rules the affair of Persia? They said: A woman. He said: A people will not prosper whose affair a woman rules."
"20783","And Abu Bakrah said: I came while the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was bowing, breathless, so I bowed before the row. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he said: Which of you bowed before the row? I said: I did. He said: May Allah increase you in eagerness, and do not repeat."
"20784","And Abu Bakrah said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you think, if Aslam and Ghifar were better than Asad and Ghatafan, do you think they lost? They said: Yes. He said: Then they are better than them. Then he said: What do you think, if Juhaynah and Muzaynah were better than the two allies, of Tamim and Amir ibn Sasah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his voice with it, do you think they lost? They said: Yes. He said: Then they are better than them."
"20785","He said, and Abu Bakrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two months of Eid do not decrease: Ramadan and Dhu al-Hijjah."
"20786","And Abu Bakrah said: A man was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man praised him with good, so the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to you, you have cut the neck of your brother. By Allah, if he heard it, he would never prosper. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you praises another, let him say: By Allah, so-and-so, and I do not declare anyone pure before Allah."
"20787","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I found this hadith in my father's book in his handwriting: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad told us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from Abu Bakrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you think, if Aslam and Ghifar were better than the two allies, Asad and Ghatafan, do you think they lost? They said: Yes. He said: Then what do you think, if Muzaynah and Juhaynah were better than Banu Tamim and Amir ibn Sasah, and Hammad raised his voice with it, imitating the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), do you think they lost? They said: Yes. He said: Then they are better than them."
"20788","Affan told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from Abu Bakrah, that Jibril, peace be upon him, said: O Muhammad, recite the Quran upon one harf. So Mikail, peace be upon him, said: Ask for more for him. So he asked for more for him. He said: Recite it upon two ahruf. Mikail said: Ask for more for him. So he asked for more for him, until it reached seven ahruf. He said: Each is healing, sufficient, as long as you do not seal a verse of punishment with mercy, or a verse of mercy with punishment, like your saying: Come and approach and come forth and go and hasten and hurry."
"20789","Affan told us, Hammad ibn Salamah told us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a covenanted soul without its right will not find the scent of Paradise, and its scent is indeed found from a distance of a hundred years."
"20790","Affan told us, Mubarak ibn Fudalah told us, from al-Hasan, Abu Bakrah informed me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray, and when he prostrated, al-Hasan would jump upon his back and upon his neck, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would lift gently lest he fall. He said: He did that more than once. When he finished his prayer, they said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you do with al-Hasan something we have not seen you do. He said: He is my sweet basil from this world, and this son of mine is a master, and perhaps Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will reconcile through him between two groups of the Muslims."
"20791","Hashim told us, al-Mubarak told us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two Muslims confront one another with their swords, both intending to kill his companion, and one of them kills the other, then both are in the Fire. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the killer, so what about the killed? He said: Because he intended to kill his companion."
"20792","And with it, Mubarak told us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A people will never prosper whom a woman rules."
"20793","Muammal told us, Hammad ibn Zayd told us, Ayyub and Yunus and Hisham and al-Mualla ibn Ziyad informed us, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two Muslims confront one another with their swords, and one of them kills his companion, then both are in the Fire together."
"20794","Muammal told us, Hammad informed us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day described the description of the Dajjal and the description of his parents. He said: The parents of the Dajjal will remain thirty years without a child being born to them, then a son will be born to them, joyful, circumcised, the least beneficial thing and the most harmful. His eyes sleep but his heart does not sleep. Then he mentioned it, except that he said: Then this one was born to us, one-eyed, joyful, circumcised, the least beneficial thing and the most harmful."
"20795","Bahz told us, Hammam told us, Qatadah informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should say: I stood all of Ramadan. Qatadah said: So Allah knows best, I fear praise for his Ummah, or he says: There must be one sleeping or heedless."
"20796","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us, Shubah told us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, he said: Abu Bakrah wrote to his son, while he was an official in Sijistan, that he should not judge between two men while angry, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No judge should judge between two, or two disputants, while he is angry."
